1
00:00:00,429 --> 00:00:01,929
(Stuart:)Where do you get off sending me

2
00:00:01,930 --> 00:00:04,130
to shop with your girlfriend?!

3
00:00:04,132 --> 00:00:05,432
(Sheldon:)I don't understand.

4
00:00:05,434 --> 00:00:06,934
(Sheldon:)You were happy to do this
when I hired you.

5
00:00:06,935 --> 00:00:08,535
Why-why are you
upset with me now?

6
00:00:08,537 --> 00:00:11,877
(Stuart:)Oh, I'm not upset with you, but
Amy's pretty bent out of shape,

7
00:00:11,874 --> 00:00:16,174
(Stuart:)so she hired me
to let you have it.

8
00:00:17,779 --> 00:00:19,949
(Sheldon:)Well, I suppose
turnabout is fair play.

9
00:00:19,948 --> 00:00:22,888
(Stuart:)You're darn right it's fair
play, you selfish jerk!

10
00:00:26,989 --> 00:00:28,259
(Amy:)You know, just when I think

11
00:00:28,257 --> 00:00:29,787
(Amy:)we're making progress
in our relationship,

12
00:00:29,791 --> 00:00:31,421
(Amy:)we revert to our old patterns

13
00:00:31,426 --> 00:00:33,126
(Amy:)where thoughts and feelings
go unexpressed.

14
00:00:33,128 --> 00:00:34,798
(Amy:)I mean, if he didn't want
to go shopping with me,

15
00:00:34,796 --> 00:00:36,266
(Amy:)why didn't he just say so?

16
00:00:36,265 --> 00:00:40,165
(Beverly:)Maybe he couldn't get
a word in edgewise.

17
00:00:42,804 --> 00:00:44,834
(Amy:)I'm sorry, I've been
going on and on.

18
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:46,470
(Beverly:)Oh, it's all right, dear.

19
00:00:46,475 --> 00:00:49,445
(Beverly:)Sheldon has a brilliant
and complicated mind.

20
00:00:49,444 --> 00:00:52,484
(Beverly:)It's understandable that being
in a relationship with him

21
00:00:52,481 --> 00:00:53,711
(Beverly:)could be trying.

22
00:00:53,715 --> 00:00:55,145
I called him “babe” once.

23
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:57,950
(Amy:)He asked me to get a drug test.

24
00:00:59,521 --> 00:01:01,421
(Beverly:)Well, I do admire your resolve.

